message: "If you use Scientific Data Simulator, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Sandner"
    given-names: "Daniel"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1041-814X"
title: "Scientific Data Simulator (scidatasim): A Modular Testbed for Synthetic Scientific Data with Open or Hidden Ground Truth"
abstract: >-
  Scientific Data Simulator (scidatasim) is a modular testbed that generates synthetic scientific
  data whose ground truth is known and kept private. It is designed for creating and managing
  reproducible scientific simulations, for applications where real data are unavailable, not yet
  available, incomplete or imprecise, or have no known ground truth. Models declare what each
  output is: a hidden quantity, an observation or a label. Observation models add the measurement
  (noise, bias, censoring, calibration). Each run records its configuration, seed, version and
  checksums. Releases bundle the public data with questions and keep the answer keys apart. A leak
  audit attacks a release before publication. Simulation studies compare methods against blind and
  naive baselines. Labels mark questions the data cannot settle, so evaluations can tell real
  inference from leaks, shortcuts, contamination and guessing. Uses include reference data for
  validating methods, benchmarks for AI systems and agents, and pre-registered predictions tested
  against data released later, such as Gaia DR4 epoch astrometry.
